{
  "about": "THE NEAR-NAME RULE (kit 0.13.5). When a shot's step names something that is not on screen, which on-screen names are near enough to offer as 'Did you mean …?'. Run by BOTH sides: the kit's NearName (NearNameSharedCasesTests.cs — the director's log line on a failed press) and the website's near-name.ts (apps/api/src/game-capture/near-name.spec.ts — the Try's 'Did you mean' and the shots list's 'name not seen in the running game yet'). DATA, not a copy of either: a disagreement is a finding for both sides. THE RULE: (1) TOKENS — a name splits at every character that is not a letter or digit, at a lower→upper step (tabHeroes), at the last capital of a capital run followed by a lower-case letter (UIButton → ui, button), and between letters and digits; each token is lower-cased per character; the synonyms below are mapped (btn → button); repeats are dropped (first kept). (2) MATCH — a one-to-one pairing of the wanted name's tokens with the candidate's: first every exact pair, then every PREFIX pair (the shorter token is at least minPrefix characters, neither is all digits, and the longer starts with it — equip ~ equipment, pet ~ pets), each pass in the wanted name's token order taking the candidate's first free token. (3) SCORE = matched / (wanted tokens + candidate tokens − matched). (4) A candidate is OFFERED only when score ≥ threshold AND at least one matched pair has NEITHER token in roleTokens — a shared 'tab'-style role word alone is never enough. (4b) SAFETY: a candidate that would be offered is REFUSED — never offered, only counted as `unsafe` — when its printed selector or its label has a press-risk root (money, deleting, resetting, the account: the ONE list in press-risk.cases.json, which the kit enforces at every gated press), or when it INTRODUCES a spend noun (a word starting with one of spendNouns that no word of the wanted name starts with: Revive_Button → Revive_Gems_Button spends gems). A one-press fix must never turn a harmless press into a spending or destroying one; when every near name is unsafe the site says 'No safe button like X' and offers no press. (5) ROWS are the kit's ui-dump rows (ReflectionCheatBridge.OnScreenRows) or bare names; a row whose printed name does not reach it (the NotReachedMarker) or that prints an index (' #i (unstable …)') is never offered. (6) FIRST, the exact answer: a row whose name equals the wanted name ignoring case (and whose label contains the wanted @label, when one is given) means 'present' — or 'locked' when every such row is [locked] — and nothing is offered. (7) ORDER: score (highest first), then unlocked before locked, then (only for a pressed name, wants=clickable) a row with a real Selectable type before a [candidate: …] or bare row, then a row whose label matches (contains the wanted @label, or shares a non-role token with the wanted name), then the printed selector by ordinal code units; one row per selector; at most max. Scores are reported rounded to 3 places. THE THRESHOLD, justified by the cases below: 0.5 keeps every real rename the cases hold (Tab_Equipment → Equip_Tab 1.0, Tab_Pets → Pet_Tab 1.0, PlayButton → Play_Btn 1.0, Equipment → Equip_Tab 0.5) and refuses the one-content-token-of-three shape (Shop_Offer / Shop_Tab 0.333, Level1 / Level10 0.333) where the second word is what tells two buttons apart; the role rule — not the number — refuses Tab / Shop_Tab (0.5).",
